id.instance: String (TS "c<n>") (not used in this chunk)
num.game: i32
num.cursor: u32 (not used in this chunk)
map.ordered: IndexMap
bag.data: IndexMap<String, serde_json::Value>
error.style: Result<_, StoreError> from every store call; the tests panic on an unexpected one and assert is_err() where TS asserted a throw
null.optional: Option + skip_serializing_if (the tests accept absent or null for a TS undefined)
null.nullable: Option, serialised null
case.json: camelCase via serde rename_all (every port value in the tests is built from and read as TS's JSON)
case.rust: snake_case
state.mut: &mut GameState writes, &GameState reads, &mut EngineSink for TS sink mutators (not used in this chunk)
rng.source: Rng::new(&state.seed, state.rng_cursor) and write the cursor back (not used in this chunk)
hook.style: Arc<dyn Fn + Send + Sync> via hook(); no fn pointers, no Box (the fake's catalog, clock and redemption hooks are Arc<dyn Fn + Send + Sync> closures)
registry.style: OnceLock set once by register_all; fused scripts built on lookup from state (not used in this chunk)
async.style: tokio in crates/server only; none in pure crates; #[tokio::test] per case
log.style: tracing JSON to stdout, server only (not used in this chunk)
store.tx: one TS store call = begin(None) + method + commit on Ok (drop = rollback on Err); a nested tx is the outer &mut Tx
store.args: &str ids, &T rows, &[T] lists, Option<&str> nullable strings, usize caps, i64 epoch ms
store.ints: epoch ms and counts i64, ratings f64, quantities i32, caps usize (read through JSON, so any width passes)
store.pg_tests: skipped unless DATABASE_URL is set; serialized on store::contract::PG_SERIAL
